What it does
Accounts: sign up, log in, and log out. Each user sees only their own schedule.
Plan your week: add events in six categories: Workout, Meal, Habit, Class, Work, and Responsibility.
Check off planned items when you complete them.
Log unplanned events, like a pickup game or a dinner out, so your week shows what really happened.
Edit and delete any event. Deleting asks "Are you sure?" first.
Star important events and see them on a Starred page.
Search, filter, and sort by category, planned or unplanned, done or not done, title, notes, and date.
Dashboard: a chart of completed versus planned items per week, plus this week's completion rate, workouts completed, and unplanned events logged.
Weekly calendar view: a Mon–Sun grid with fixed commitments in gray and healthy items in color.
Recurring routines: set something once (e.g., "Tue 6am rower intervals") and it appears every week.
Conflict warning: you get a warning if you plan something on top of a class or work block.
How to use it
Sign up for an account.
Add your classes and work shifts for the week.
Add routines for things you do every week, like a training plan.
Plan meals, workouts, and habits into your open time.
Check items off as you finish them, and use Log unplanned for anything extra.
Open the dashboard to see how closely your week matched your plan.
